# pnpm + Metro (Expo SDK 57) resolution notes:
#
# Metro resolves imports by walking node_modules from the importing file —
# through pnpm's symlinked .pnpm layout, a package's deps are visible only
# inside its own .pnpm/<pkg>/node_modules. That works for declared deps, but
# two classes of packages broke in practice (M4, twice — see
# docs/M4_VERIFICATION.md):
#
#   1. react-native's runtime deps (base64-js, …) after `pnpm add` reshuffles
#      which packages earn a root-level link.
#   2. @expo/metro-runtime from expo-router/entry-classic.js.
#
# public-hoist-pattern puts these at the root where Metro's resolver always
# finds them, regardless of reshuffles. Patterns are scoped to the packages
# that actually broke rather than a blanket shamefully-hoist, to keep jest's
# transformIgnorePatterns (tuned for the pnpm layout) meaningful.
public-hoist-pattern[]=*eslint*
public-hoist-pattern[]=*prettier*
public-hoist-pattern[]=base64-js
public-hoist-pattern[]=@expo/*
public-hoist-pattern[]=react-native*
public-hoist-pattern[]=eventemitter3
